# Per-project overrides for the .test setup (managed by chezmoi).
#
# This file is deliberately all comments. It exists so that the
# `import sites/*.caddy` line in ../Caddyfile always matches at least one
# file — caddy complains about a glob that matches nothing — and so the
# override syntax is documented where you go looking for it.
#
# Drop a new <project>.caddy next to this one; the files here are yours, not
# chezmoi's, so they are not tracked in the dotfiles repo. An exact hostname
# always beats the wildcard *.test block, whatever the filenames sort to.
#
# The wildcard only serves ~/Sites/laravel/<project>/public, so a project that
# lives anywhere else under ~/Sites (github/, shopify_themes/, tries/) needs a
# file here to get a hostname at all — that is the main reason to write one.
#
# Pin one project to PHP 8.3 (9083 is the 8.3 socket; 9084 is the default):
#
#   legacy.test {
#   	tls internal
#   	root * /home/saiful/Sites/laravel/legacy/public
#   	php_fastcgi 127.0.0.1:9083
#   	file_server
#   }
#
# A project outside ~/Sites/laravel, or one that is not a Laravel app — serve
# the repo root, no public/:
#
#   docs.test {
#   	tls internal
#   	root * /home/saiful/Sites/github/docs
#   	file_server browse
#   }
#
# Hand a hostname to a dev server that is already running (vite, node):
#
#   spa.test {
#   	tls internal
#   	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:5173
#   }
#
# After editing: systemctl --user restart caddy-dev  (only if it is running;
# otherwise the next request picks the change up on its own).
